# cuts/v1.0.52/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# 🔴 THIS HEADER WAS v1.0.51's, VERBATIM, AND MOST OF IT WAS FALSE HERE.
# scripts/new_cut.sh opens a cut by COPYING its parent, so this file arrived
# describing the previous cut: line 1 named cuts/v1.0.51/cut.env, the body
# explained why CM051 was pinned at a8cfee86 while the assignment below sets
# cef9c20c, and the v1.0.52 note was appended at the bottom as a footnote to a
# document that contradicted it. Thirteen lines said v1.0.51 and two said
# v1.0.52. Found by @TNM.
#
# NONE OF IT WAS LOAD-BEARING FOR THE PARSER -- the three assignments at the
# foot are all any reader consumes, and they were correct throughout. That is
# exactly why it was worth fixing rather than shrugging at: a wrong comment in
# a cut record is invisible to every gate and permanent in the artefact's
# provenance. The next person to read this file to answer "what was in v1.0.52"
# would have been told about v1.0.51.
#
# 🔴 ONE CLAIM WAS NOT MERELY STALE BUT ACTIVELY WRONG, and it concerned the
# pin's own safety argument. The inherited text asserted "the last commit to
# touch install.sh is c93e0f83 (#1269)". For THIS cut that is false: install.sh
# moved twice more, and those two moves ARE the reason this cut exists. The
# inherited paragraph therefore argued the pin was safe using a premise that
# had already expired. Re-measured at origin/main:
#
#   commits v1.0.51..cef9c20c                        13
#   of those, touching install.sh                     2   cce32b41, 19fd3931
#   last install.sh commit at or before the pin       19fd3931 (#1289)
#   commits cef9c20c..origin/main touching install.sh  0
#   CONTROL: total commits in that same range          2   <- so the 0 above is
#                                                             a real absence and
#                                                             not an empty range
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 DAEMON_COMMIT NAMES THE ARTEFACT, NOT THE TREE. DO NOT "UPDATE" IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Carried UNCHANGED from v1.0.50 at f1c7c57d, and it must not be advanced.
# THIS CUT REBUILDS NO DAEMON. Both fixes it carries are in install.sh, which is
# CM051's own file; nothing under crates/ or web/ is touched, so cut.env's own
# rule -- any path that reaches the artefact forces a rebuild -- is not
# triggered.
#
# If a later reader finds oa main ahead of this pin, the correct response is NOT
# to advance this line. It is to ask whether the daemon must be REBUILT. The
# artefact is the fact; the tree is the claim; when they disagree, change the
# claim. Editing this line to match a moved tree is how a cut acquires false
# provenance, which is the v1.0.14 failure.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 -- WHY cef9c20c, AND WHY IT SURVIVES ITS OWN WITNESS LANDING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 names the tree whose install.sh SHIPS, compared by BLOB IDENTITY and not
# by ancestry (verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh self-test 6). Measured:
#
#   install.sh @ cef9c20c   0e5b7a7ca3591809b2e39f870e3952bd6c715329
#   install.sh @ origin/main 0e5b7a7ca3591809b2e39f870e3952bd6c715329   IDENTICAL
#
# cef9c20c is main immediately after the two shipping fixes landed: #1283 (the
# vane-pull warning) and #1289 (the secrets directory's own 0700).
#
# 🔴 THE TWO-PR RULE DOES NOT BIND HERE, AND THE REASON IS MEASURED, NOT
# ASSUMED. v1.0.46's header records that a pin and the WITNESS to that pin
# cannot ride the same commit, because bundling them leaves CM051= naming a tree
# whose install.sh no longer exists on main. That hazard exists only when
# install.sh is MOVING. It is not moving now: zero commits touch install.sh
# between the pin and main, against a control of two commits in that range. The
# installer version bump (#1295) and this file's own edit are both non-install.sh
# paths. So the blob at cef9c20c is the blob on main, and the pin stays true
# across its own landing. A MEASURED exemption, not a waiver.
#
# ⚠️ IT BECOMES BINDING THE MOMENT ANYTHING TOUCHES install.sh. If a further PR
# lands on install.sh before the tag, this pin is stale and re-running
# verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh is mandatory, not optional. v1.0.46's header says
# it plainly and it is repeated here because it already happened once: "a pin
# chosen early and trusted is a pin that goes stale while you are not looking".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT CARRIES, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CARRIES. Thirteen commits landed since v1.0.51 and exactly TWO reach the
# customer. Both are in install.sh, both are mutation-tested against their own
# pre-fix parent, and both hold a row in cut-manifests/v1.0.52.yaml:
#   #1283  the 3.5GB vane pull warns BEFORE the pipe swallows its progress,
#          and the comment that claimed otherwise is corrected  (board #544)
#   #1289  the store-credential DIRECTORY carries its own 0700, not merely a
#          0600 file inside a 0755 directory  (board #549/#550 class)
#
# THE OTHER ELEVEN IMPROVED THE MEASUREMENT, NOT THE PRODUCT: probe fixes, CI,
# the walk record, the registry. They are real and merged and deliberately NOT
# written as manifest rows -- a row claims the artefact contains the fix, and
# eleven rows that can never go green would sit at landed=no forever. That is
# the #1268 lesson and it is why this cut's manifest has two entries.
#
# DOES NOT CARRY, stated so the walk is not a surprise:
#   #547  identity_resolver spins at 100% CPU forever on an empty dataset and
#         is orphaned to PPID 1 after install.sh exits "successfully"
#   #543  the consent screen may tell the customer that declining public
#         look-ups stops Wikidata/MusicBrainz/OpenLibrary contact, while the
#         one-shot enrichment pass is not gated by that answer
#   #519  3 of 23 LaunchAgents are never loaded and install.sh reports success,
#         because `launchctl load` exits 0 on failure
#   #509  `launchctl kickstart -k` blocks on a penalty-boxed job, 5 call sites
# The freshness, grounding and usage-journal probes WILL therefore still fail
# this walk. That is expected and is not a reason to withhold the cut: the walk
# gates PROMOTION, not assembly.
#
# 🔻 BOTH MANIFEST ROWS CARRY capability_id=none, so verify_must_contain.sh
# reports them and does not fail the cut. Both changes are UNGUARDED by
# capability_matrix.sh and can regress silently. Written here rather than left
# to be discovered later; naming them is owed and is tracked, not waived.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE, AND THAT IS CORRECT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.52.tsv does not exist, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly not conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release is a
# prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to its current target.
# The sequence is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote. A green cut is not
# a shipped one, and nothing between "gates green" and "customer download" is a
# runtime proof until a walker runs it.
#
# ⚠️ BEFORE THE WALK, ONE PRECAUTION THAT COSTS NOTHING (TNM, 2026-08-29):
# put the DMG in the WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks in only
# three directories of the ssh user it walks as -- $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop
# and $HOME -- and on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES
# artefact_sha256_source to read measured(...) and exits 2 otherwise. That
# CLEAN-scoped block has never executed in this project's history, because there
# has never been a clean record. A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere would
# produce PROMOTE=0 for a reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than
# "wrong folder", on the one run where everyone is tired and reading the verdict
# instead of the field.

CUT_VERSION=1.0.52
DAEMON_COMMIT=f1c7c57d
CM051=cef9c20cedab23e9d44ffd0b9ba5e6d34f90f131
